.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt VEDI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vedi
.Nd page colored text, select it with the keyboard, copy it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm
.Fl \-completion Ar shell
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
pages terminal output.
SGR colors and attributes, 24-bit color included, and OSC 8 hyperlinks are
drawn as the terminal would.
Shift with the arrows, or the mouse, selects text, and Ctrl+c copies it as
plain text.
With no
.Ar file
it reads standard input.
A file that changes on disk is read again, so a log that grows is followed.
.Pp
Flags in the
.Ev VEDI
environment variable apply to every run; the command line wins.
Each setting flag has a line in the config file, see
.Sx FILES ;
the flag overrides it for one run.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl S , Fl \-wrap , Fl \-no\-wrap
Wrap long lines;
.Fl S
is
.Fl \-no\-wrap .
Default: on.
.It Fl \-wrap\-style Ar style
Wrap at the screen's edge
.Pq Cm char ,
or at words
.Pq Cm word .
Default:
.Cm char .
.It Fl F , Fl \-quit\-if\-one\-page , Fl \-no\-quit\-if\-one\-page
Print the text and quit if it fits the screen, as
.Xr cat 1
would; the pager opens only for more.
Default: off.
.It Fl \-one\-page\-rows\-below Ar n
Rows
.Fl F
leaves below the text, for the shell's prompt.
Default: 1.
.It Fl \-auto\-reload , Fl \-no\-auto\-reload
Read a file again when it changes on disk.
Default: on.
.It Cm +G
Start at the last line and follow until end of file.
.It Cm + Ns Ar n
Start with line
.Ar n
at the top.
.It Fl \-scrolled\-by Ar n
Start on the last screenful, scrolled
.Ar n
rows up.
.It Fl \-cursor\-row Ar n
Put the cursor on row
.Ar n
of the last screenful.
.It Fl \-cursor\-col Ar n
Put the cursor in column
.Ar n
of the last screenful.
.It Fl \-clipboard\-cmd Ar cmd
Pipe copied text to
.Ar cmd
instead of writing it with OSC 52.
.It Fl \-no\-clipboard\-cmd
Copy with OSC 52, or
.Xr pbcopy 1
in Terminal.app.
.It Fl \-open\-cmd Ar cmd
Read each file by running
.Ar cmd ,
with
.Ql %s
replaced by the file's name, or the name as the last argument.
.It Fl \-no\-open\-cmd
Read each file as it is.
.It Fl \-tab\-width Ar n
Draw a tab as
.Ar n
cells.
Default: 8.
.It Fl \-edge\-markers , Fl \-no\-edge\-markers
Mark text off the sides of the screen with
.Ql <
and
.Ql > ,
and a row that wraps with
.Ql \e .
Default: off.
.It Fl \-file\-separators , Fl \-no\-file\-separators
With several inputs, draw a row naming each.
Default: on.
.It Fl \-status\-line , Fl \-no\-status\-line
Draw the status line; off, only for a prompt or a message.
Default: on.
.It Fl \-view\-style Ar style
Draw the text in color
.Pq Cm color ,
without
.Pq Cm plain ,
or with its escapes as text
.Pq Cm raw .
Default:
.Cm color .
.It Fl \-config Ar file
Read the config from
.Ar file .
.It Fl \-completion Ar shell
Print the completion script for
.Cm bash ,
.Cm zsh
or
.Cm fish
and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl \-version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh KEYS
The defaults.
.Ic h
shows those in effect; the config file rebinds any of them.
.Ic Cmd+
keys are macOS only, where the terminal passes them on.
.Bl -tag -width "Ctrl+c, Cmd+c, y" -compact
.It Ic Up , Ic Down , Ic Left , Ic Right , Ic Home , Ic End , Ic j , Ic k , \
Ic 0 , Ic $ , Ic Cmd+Left , Ic Cmd+Right
Move the cursor.
.It Ic PgDn , Ic Space , Ic f , Ic Ctrl+f , Ic Ctrl+v
Down a page.
.It Ic PgUp , Ic b , Ic Ctrl+b , Ic Alt+v
Up a page.
.It Ic d , Ic Ctrl+d
Down half a page.
.It Ic u , Ic Ctrl+u
Up half a page.
.It Ic Ctrl+Left , Ic Ctrl+Right , Ic Alt+Left , Ic Alt+Right , Ic Alt+b , \
Ic Alt+f
Move by word.
.It Ic g , Ic G , Ic < , Ic > , Ic Cmd+Up , Ic Cmd+Down
First line, last line.
.It Ic T , Ic M , Ic B
Top, middle, bottom row of the screen.
.It Ic \&[ , Ic \&]
Previous, next input or title.
.It Ic J , Ic K , Ic Shift+Up , Ic Shift+Down , Ic Shift+Left , \
Ic Shift+Right , Ic Shift+Home , Ic Shift+End , Ic Cmd+Shift+Left , \
Ic Cmd+Shift+Right , Ic Cmd+Shift+Up , Ic Cmd+Shift+Down
Extend the selection.
.It Ic Shift+PgUp , Ic Shift+PgDn
Extend by a page.
.It Ic Ctrl+Shift+Left , Ic Ctrl+Shift+Right , Ic Alt+Shift+Left , \
Ic Alt+Shift+Right
Extend by word.
.It Ic Ctrl+a , Ic Cmd+a
Select all.
.It Ic Esc
Clear the selection, then the search highlight.
.It Ic Ctrl+c , Ic Cmd+c , Ic y
Copy the selection as plain text.
.It Ic Enter
Copy the selection and quit; with none, down a line.
.It Ic /
Search; ignores case unless capitalized; empty repeats.
.It Ic \&?
Search backward.
.It Ic n , Ic N , Ic Cmd+g , Ic Cmd+Shift+g
Next and previous match;
.Ic \&?
swaps them.
.It Ic \&:
Command prompt; see
.Sx COMMANDS .
.It Ic w
Toggle wrap.
.It Ic R
Reload the file.
.It Ic O
Toggle reading through
.Cm open_cmd .
.It Ic q
Quit.
.It Ic h
Show the key bindings.
.El
.Pp
Click and drag select; a double-click the word, a triple-click the line.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ic \&:
opens a prompt on the status line.
It takes any setting of the config file but
.Cm clipboard_cmd ,
.Cm open_cmd
and
.Cm one_page_rows_below ,
for the rest of the run, and these:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar n , Cm goto Ar n
Go to line
.Ar n .
.It Cm cycle Ar setting
Step a setting to its next value, the first after the last:
.Cm wrap , Cm wrap_style , Cm edge_markers , Cm file_separators ,
.Cm auto_reload , Cm status_line , Cm view_style
or
.Cm open_cmd .
.It Cm map Ar key action
Bind a key, as in the config file.
.It Cm help , Cm reload , Cm quit
What
.Ic h ,
.Ic R
and
.Ic q
do.
.It Cm write Ar file
Save the text as shown, or the selection, to a new file;
.Cm write!
replaces one that exists.
.El
.Pp
Tab completes the word; Up and Down recall earlier commands.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.It Ev VEDI
Flags read before the command line, split as a shell would.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the config file is looked for, instead of
.Pa ~/.config .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/vedi/vedi.conf
One directive per line; blank lines and
.Ql #
comments are skipped.
A setting is its flag with
.Ql _
for
.Ql \- :
.Cm wrap , Cm wrap_style , Cm tab_width , Cm edge_markers , Cm file_separators ,
.Cm auto_reload , Cm status_line , Cm view_style , Cm one_page_rows_below ,
.Cm clipboard_cmd
and
.Cm open_cmd ,
which a glob before the command limits to the files it matches.
.Cm map Ar key action
binds a key, later lines winning, and the action
.Cm none
unbinds;
.Cm clear_all_shortcuts
drops every binding so far, the defaults included.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
As the pager for the shell, git and man:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
export PAGER="vedi \-F"
export MANPAGER="sh \-c \(aqcol \-bx | vedi \-F\(aq"
.Ed
.Pp
Where OSC 52 does not reach the clipboard:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
vedi \-\-clipboard\-cmd \(aqxclip \-selection clipboard\(aq build.log
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr less 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/dlh/vedi
